NOTICE — dhoby-ghaut
====================

Relicense: GPL-3.0-only -> AGPL-3.0-only (2026-10-05)
------------------------------------------------------

Until 2026-10-05 this crate was licensed GPL-3.0-only through
`license.workspace = true`. On 2026-10-05, at the maintainer's explicit
direction (GitHub #561, #562), it was relicensed AGPL-3.0-only so that it can
depend on `kovan`, which is AGPL-3.0-only (see `crates/kovan/NOTICE`).

Why: the high-fidelity workbench reads and writes kovan-compatible files (its
recipes, i.e. input decks, are kovan markdown + TOML artifacts) and shows
literature through kovan. The maintainer decided that every input and output
file of Dhoby Ghaut is kovan-compatible and that the crate depends on `kovan`
directly. A GPLv3 crate linking AGPLv3 code would be a combined work carrying
AGPL's network clause anyway (GPLv3 §13); licensing the crate AGPL-3.0-only
outright removes the cross-licence question, as `kovan` itself did.

`dhoby-ghaut` was published at no version before this change (0.0.1 in
`Cargo.toml`, never released), so there is no earlier GPL release to
grandfather. No file in this crate carries ported third-party code: the
examples cite upstream projects (pyDOSEIA, TRISO-ATOPS) only to describe what
the workspace's own ports do.

Dependency: kovan
------------------

  Crate:    kovan (path dependency, `../kovan`, default features off)
  License:  AGPL-3.0-only
  Gating:   not on wasm32 (the browser demos build this library for wasm)

`kovan` is declared in this crate's own `Cargo.toml`, not in the workspace
`[workspace.dependencies]`, so no other crate can pick it up by accident.

Consequence for downstream crates
---------------------------------

Any crate that depends on `dhoby-ghaut` as a library now links AGPL-3.0-only
code. Re-read this NOTICE and confirm with the maintainer before adding one.

